DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ggeettggrroouupplliisstt() function scans the group database (see ggrroouupp(5)) to
       obtain the list of groups that _u_s_e_r belongs  to.   Up  to  _*_n_g_r_o_u_p_s  of
       these groups are returned in the array _g_r_o_u_p_s.

       If  it was not among the groups defined for _u_s_e_r in the group database,
       then _g_r_o_u_p is included in the  list  of  groups  returned  by  ggeettggrroouu‐‐
       pplliisstt();  typically this argument is specified as the group ID from the
       password record for _u_s_e_r.

       The _n_g_r_o_u_p_s argument is a value‐result argument: on  return  it  always
       contains  the  number  of  groups found for _u_s_e_r, including _g_r_o_u_p; this
       value may be greater than the number of groups stored in _g_r_o_u_p_s.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       If the number of groups of which _u_s_e_r is a member is less than or equal
       to _*_n_g_r_o_u_p_s, then the value _*_n_g_r_o_u_p_s is returned.

       If the user is a member of more than  _*_n_g_r_o_u_p_s  groups,  then  ggeettggrroouu‐‐
       pplliisstt()  returns  -1.  In this case, the value returned in _*_n_g_r_o_u_p_s can
       be used to resize the buffer passed  to  a  further  call  to  ggeettggrroouu‐‐
       pplliisstt().

